# TASK-260715-2d3g5e tester handoff

## Outcome

Implemented one candidate-neutral Swift Testing suite with candidate selection as data. The libssh2 registration executes the production LibSSH2TransportFactory through the real OpenSSH loopback harness. The repository has no ReluxNIOSSH SSHTransport adapter target, so every ReluxNIOSSH M0, cancellation, and deferred-state row is retained as an explicit Swift Testing known issue instead of a green fixture.

## Inventory

- 9 M0 functional rows per candidate: integration/injection, host and auth policy, direct/exec/upload isolation, bounded buffers/backpressure/windows, client and server rekey, keepalive, lifecycle, privacy-safe errors, and mandatory metrics.
- 15 explicit cancellation or timeout cleanup scopes per candidate: resolution, connect, initial KEX, host decision, credential lookup, authentication, open, read, write, EOF, exec, upload, rekey, keepalive, and close.
- All four M3 semantics assert explicit states and owner TASK-260728-3cveay. Libssh2 runtime reports unsupported or notReported, including receive windows, RFC open reason, exec status/signal coreDumped, KEX generation, server-rekey fields, and keepalive deep telemetry.

## Validation

- swift test: exit 0; 434 tests in 37 suites; 25 known issues, all limited to the absent ReluxNIOSSH adapter.
- Focused conformance coverage run: exit 0.
- Affected files coverage: 84.02 percent regions, 95.11 percent functions, 92.56 percent lines.
- swift format lint --recursive Sources Tests Package.swift: exit 0.
- scripts/check-core-boundaries.sh: exit 0.
- swift build: exit 0.
- git diff --check: exit 0.

## Regressions fixed during validation

- Concurrent write/EOF fixture now waits until all four write operations are admitted before half-close.
- Channel pressure fixture uses a deterministic sleeping subprocess so the 65th operation reliably proves the hard cap.
- Complete available metric counter and bounded-gauge reconciliation plus every libssh2 deferred runtime surface are asserted.

## Candidate evidence

- libssh2: green for the executed M0 inventory and explicit M3 states.
- ReluxNIOSSH: red/unavailable because no production adapter target exists; no candidate behavior was emulated or waived.
