+# TASK-260715-2d3g5e reviewer handoff
+
+## Verdict
+
+CHANGES REQUESTED. Route to `to-dev`; there is no external blocker.
+
+## Blocking findings
+
+1. The required conformance tests are not green or deterministic. `swift test --filter SSHTransportConformanceTests` exited 1. The libssh2 `directExecUploadAndChannelIsolation` M0 row and the `write` cancellation row both failed at `LibSSH2AdapterIntegrationTests.swift:501` because `pendingWrites` did not reach four within 200 scheduler yields. A focused `swift test --filter concurrentSameChannelWrites` repeated the same failure and exited 1. This contradicts the attached exit-0 evidence and fails the deterministic-tests and tests-green gates.
+2. The production `clientAndServerRekey` row does not test server-initiated rekey. `SSHTransportConformanceTests.swift:174-178` invokes protected-byte client rekey, fake-clock client rekey, explicit client rekey coalescing, and admission timeout only. Repository search found no production server-triggered KEX fixture or test. The M0 requirement that inbound server KEX preserve active traffic therefore has no explicit assertion.
+3. Several advertised cancellation rows do not exercise cancellation at the named site or assert repeated return to the complete resource baseline. In `SSHTransportConformanceTests.swift:201-232`, `hostDecision` calls host-ordering, `channelOpen` calls rekey-admission timeout, `eof` and `exec` share a channel failure/timeout test, and `keepalive` calls a fatal-failure test. This does not establish deterministic cancellation for every reviewed wait or repeated restoration of tasks, channels, sockets, descriptors, and buffers.
+
+## Candidate and M3 evidence
+
+- The same parameterized suite inventory selects libssh2 and ReluxNIOSSH as data. Libssh2 executes the production adapter. ReluxNIOSSH remains explicit known-issue/red evidence because no `SSHTransport` adapter target exists.
+- Libssh2 explicitly asserts all four M3 capability states as `unsupported`, validates runtime `unsupported`/`notReported` surfaces, and maps ownership to `TASK-260728-3cveay`.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `swift test --filter SSHTransportConformanceTests`: exit 1; 2 unexpected failures plus 25 expected known issues.
+- `swift test --filter concurrentSameChannelWrites`: exit 1; deterministic failure at line 501.
+- `swift format lint --recursive Sources Tests Package.swift`: exit 0.
+- `./scripts/check-core-boundaries.sh`: exit 0.
+- `git diff --check`: exit 0.
+- Coverage was not re-accepted because the affected gate is failing; the previously attached 84.02% region figure does not satisfy the passing-coverage DoD while tests are red.
+
+## Required rework
+
+- Replace the scheduler-yield admission assertion with deterministic synchronization and make the focused and full conformance runs pass.
+- Add a real server-initiated KEX fixture/test with byte-exact active traffic assertions for loss, duplication, ordering, and bounded buffering.
+- Add actual candidate-adapter cancellation/timeout injection at every named wait and repeat each cleanup cycle against a full resource baseline.
+- Refresh the task outcome with new commands, real exit codes, test inventory, and coverage after all gates are green.
